# Extra known failures when the guest runs under QEMU TCG on a slow host
# (hosted CI runners), merged with qemutest.xfail via a second --xfail.
#
# These four tests are timer-driven (alarm/setitimer/signal timing).  On a
# runner where TCG needs about five minutes just to reach login:, they print
# their TAP plan and never see their alarm fire; the guest itself stays
# responsive and the next test runs.  They pass on KVM and on a fast TCG
# host.  Bounded to two minutes so a stall costs little.  Roadmap: T1,
# tick-based timers under a host that steals most of the guest's time.
1:120 flaky
5:120 flaky
37:120 flaky
41:120 flaky
